{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Or to serve the sun, or the moon, or any of the host of heaven, which I have not commanded.</b> It is well known that the Holy One, blessed be He, did not command the worship of idolatry; if so, what reason is there to say 'which I have not commanded'?" "<b>And by way of</b> the plain sense (peshat): because the worshippers of the sun and the moon and the other celestial forces think that through their worship they will find favor in the eyes of HaShem, exalted be He, since they are the ministers of the King, and one who honors the King's ministers thereby honors the King — therefore it was necessary to say 'which I have not commanded,' for He did not command this honor. Or the sense of 'which I have not commanded' may be as if it said 'which I commanded by way of prohibition,' that is, the prohibition (Exodus 20:5) לא תשתחוה להם — 'you shall not bow down to them.' And similar to it, in my opinion, is (Deuteronomy 32) שחת לו לא — 'he has corrupted himself by no' — as though it says לא as a negation; and I shall mention this when I reach that place, with the help of HaShem." "<b>And by way of</b> the Kabbalah: the addition of the words 'which I have not commanded' is with regard to the fact that He commanded us to keep His covenant, and Scripture says 'who did the evil to transgress the covenant' — the covenant of Sinai, as it is written (Exodus 19:5): ״ועתה אם שמוע תשמעו בקולי ושמרתם את בריתי״, and this covenant is the attribute of day and the attribute of night. And according to this interpretation, even though I commanded him in the daily offering to offer two lambs, one in the morning and one in the evening, which correspond to the attribute of day and the attribute of night that channel light and power into the two luminaries, which are the sun and the moon — 'I did not command' to worship the sun and the moon. And understand this."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {1 "The phrase שחת לו לא appears in Deuteronomy 32:5; the author writes דברים לב (chapter only); normalized citation could include verse 5 but author did not specify it."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:48:57.456015156Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}